Ammo.js — Bullet Physics (btRaycastVehicle etc.) compiled to WebAssembly.
Source: https://github.com/kripken/ammo.js (builds/ammo.wasm.{js,wasm}, main branch)
License: zlib License (Bullet Physics / ammo.js) — permissive, redistribution OK.
Header of ammo.wasm.js: "This is ammo.js, a port of Bullet Physics to JavaScript. zlib licensed."

Bundled here for runtime physics via PlayCanvas (pc.WasmModule.getInstance('Ammo'));
no CDN fetch at runtime. Files:
  - ammo.wasm.js   (Emscripten glue; defines global `Ammo` factory)  ~441 KB
  - ammo.wasm.wasm (WebAssembly Bullet build; includes btRaycastVehicle) ~731 KB

Why this specific build (not three.js's examples copy): PlayCanvas'
RigidBodyComponentSystem.onLibraryLoaded() calls `Ammo.addFunction(...)` to wire
the internal collision-tick callback. The kripken/ammo.js `builds/ammo.wasm.js`
exports `addFunction` (built with the emscripten runtime method exported);
three.js's slimmer examples build does NOT, and PlayCanvas throws on it. Verified
this build exports addFunction + btRaycastVehicle + btDefaultVehicleRaycaster +
btVehicleTuning (required for the official raycast-vehicle pattern [C-veh]).
